    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.13 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nBugs are getting crazier and crazier 😳\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da2c0a2f-3b6b-4eec-acd6-fe79a2154b31\n\n`v:count` is lost in mappings with defined `mini.clue` trigger when used while `ui2` is shown as the `msg` target.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1825+g402a494f47\n```\n\n<details><summary>See the comment below</summary>\n\n```\nnvim --noplugin -u repro.lua repro.lua\n5gm\nPrints 0 instead of 5\n```\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gm\", function()\n  vim.print(vim.v.count) -- Prints 0\nend)\n\nvim.pack.add({\n  -- { src = \"https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig\" },\n  { src = \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\" },\n})\n\nlocal MiniClue = require(\"mini.clue\")\nMiniClue.setup({\n  triggers = {\n    { mode = { \"n\", \"x\" }, keys = \"g\" },\n  },\n})\n\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({\n  msg = {\n    targets = {\n      progress = \"msg\",\n      -- [\"^lsp\"] = \"msg\",\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nlocal timer = assert(vim.uv.new_timer())\ntimer:start(0, 100, function()\n  vim.schedule(function()\n    vim.api.nvim_echo({ { \"Emulate LspProgress...\" } }, false, {\n      id = \"test\",\n      kind = \"progress\",\n      status = \"running\",\n      source = \"uv.timer\",\n    })\n  end)\nend)\n\n-- vim.lsp.enable(\"lua_ls\")\n-- -- From `:h LspProgress`\n-- vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"LspProgress\", {\n--   callback = function(ev)\n--     local value = ev.data.params.value\n--     vim.api.nvim_echo({ { value.message or \"done\" } }, false, {\n--       id = \"lsp.\" .. ev.data.params.token,\n--       kind = \"progress\",\n--       source = \"vim.lsp\",\n--       title = value.title,\n--       status = value.kind ~= \"end\" and \"running\" or \"success\",\n--       percent = value.percentage,\n--     })\n--   end,\n-- })\n```\n\n</details>",
