            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can reproduce. The issue also doesn't seem to be a side effect of using `vim.print`. Please, prefer using actual logging instead. As well as not using `src` in `vim.pack.add` if not needed and not adding extra comments not directly related to the issue. Here is the reworked repro I used:\n\n```lua\n-- Target mapping\n_G.log = {}\nvim.keymap.set('n', 'gm', function() table.insert(_G.log, vim.v.count) end)\n\n-- mini.nvim\nvim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim' })\nrequire('mini.clue').setup({\n  triggers = {\n    { mode = { 'n', 'x' }, keys = 'g' },\n  },\n})\n\n-- `ui2`\nrequire('vim._core.ui2').enable({ msg = { targets = { progress = 'msg' } } })\n\nlocal timer = assert(vim.uv.new_timer())\nlocal progress_opts = { id = 'test', kind = 'progress', status = 'running', source = 'uv.timer' }\nlocal cb = vim.schedule_wrap(function() vim.api.nvim_echo({ { 'Progress...' } }, false, progress_opts) end)\n\n_G.start = function() timer:start(0, 100, cb) end\n_G.finish = function() timer:stop() end\n```\n\nWith this:\n- `2gm` adds `2` to the `_G.log`.\n- `:lua start()` and `3gm` adds `0` to the `_G.log`.\n- `:lua finish()` and `4gm` adds `4` again to the log.\n\nI'll take a look.",
